PE 677: Coloured Graphs

Small n verification:
  g(1) = 3 (expect 3? actually PE doesn't give g(1))
  g(2) = 5 (expect 5)
  g(3) = 15 (expect 15)
  g(4) = 57 (expect 57)

Known values:
  g(2) = 5
  g(3) = 15
  g(4) = 57
  g(10) = 710249
  g(100) ≡ 919747298 (mod 1000000007)

Tree shape analysis:
  n=1: 1 node (3 colors) = 3
  n=2: edge, 2 symmetric nodes -> 5 colorings
  n=3: path, center vs leaves -> 15 colorings
  n=4: 2 shapes (path + star) -> 57 colorings
